A developer raises a PR with a vulnerable package and a security check fails. What is the ideal way to handle it?
I would treat the security scan as a mandatory quality gate in the CI/CD pipeline.
If a developer raises a PR containing a vulnerable dependency, I would block the merge and notify the developer with the package name, CVE ID, and severity.
I would ask the developer to upgrade the dependency to a secure version or apply an approved mitigation. Once the fix is committed, the pipeline automatically reruns the security scan.
Only after the security checks pass and the required approvals are completed would I allow the PR to merge.
For exceptions, I would follow a formal risk-acceptance process with security-team approval and a defined expiry date.
My goal is to implement Shift-Left Security, identifying and fixing vulnerabilities as early as possible in the development lifecycle.
